# Yeti, the January head (ticket 45): the Abominable Snowman, a big shaggy white head with a frozen snarl, jagged teeth, icicles on the chin,
# a heavy brow over deep-set eyes and a thick snowy mantle round the neck. About 0.5 m wide and 0.5 m tall, twice a human head, so it
# reads at range: white fur against a grey-blue face, a dark open maw, ivory fangs.
# Frame (the soldier's head_top socket, ticket 43): the origin is the socket, 1.815 m over the soles; the head faces +Z, +Y is up. The
# neck ends at y=-0.246 (1.569 m); the mantle's underside sits at -0.27 and hides the join over the collar. The head turns on the Head
# bone, 0.25 m under the origin, so it nods from the neck. The eyes are the machines' eye part (eye_machine, a 12 cm ball meshed coarse) at half size, meshed once, used twice.
# Detail 0.95 (a head this small gets few cells at the default resolution): about 3.3k triangles of head and 2 x 300 of eyes at LOD0.
format 1

# No collider (the hit shape of the head is a number in MonsterHeads), and never culled before 200 m: the head is what reads at range
collider none
cull 200

Detail detail=0.95
    Part part=yeti_head
